body_text:
The problem is that the data contains both double quotes " and embedded trailing newlines. You want to strip the trailing newlines, and disable quoting in the CSV writer. Disable quoting quote_style="never" is how to disable quoting. Strip trailing newlines Note the trailing 
 from the data is still there, so you end up with mixed line endings. ( 

 ) .strip_chars_end("
") can be used to remove it before sinking.

Try matching on: See: regex101 Then you can just join the strings: Explanation ( ... ) : To group 1 capture [^\d.
]+ : Anything that is neighter a digit, a dot or a linebreak. Between the item and the value you find [^\S
]* : zero or more times a space that is no newline \.{3,} : followed by at least 3 dots [^\S
]* : again zero or more non newline spaces. Then match the amount ( ... ) : and capture to group 2 \d+.\d+ : any digits that must be separated by a comma
